[01:09.61] Procession moves on, the shouting is over
[01:16.68] Praise to the glory of loved ones now gone
[01:24.67] Talking aloud as they sit round their tables
[01:31.82] 
[01:34.09] Scattering flowers washed down by the rain
[01:41.31] 
[01:44.31] Stood by the gate at the foot of the garden
[01:51.90] Watching them pass like clouds in the sky
[01:58.10] 
[02:01.62] Try to cry out in the heat of the moment
[02:08.62] 
[02:10.69] Possessed by a fury that burns from inside
[02:18.16] 
[03:29.66] Cry like a child, though these years make me older
[03:36.62] With children my time is so wastefully spent
[03:43.99] 
[03:46.03] A burden to keep, though their inner communion
[03:54.85] Accept like a curse an unlucky deal
[04:01.99] 
[04:04.00] Played by the gate at the foot of the garden
[04:12.61] My view stretches out from the fence to the wall
[04:21.14] No words could explain, no actions determine
[04:29.40] Just watching the trees and the leaves as they fall
[04:35.25] 